{number: 86}
{title: Jesus, Saviour, Pilot Me}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Jesus, Savior, [F] pilot [C] me
Over life's tem-[G7] pestuous [C] sea;
Unknown waves be-[F] fore me [C] roll,
Hiding rock and [G7] treacherous [C] shoal;
Chart and compass [F] come from [C] Thee,
Jesus, Savior, [G7] pilot [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] As a mother [F] stills her [C] child,
Thou canst hush the [G7] ocean [C] wild;
Boisterous waves o-[F] bey Thy [C] will
When Thou biddest [G7] to them "Be [C] still."
Wondrous sovereign [F] of the [C] sea,
Jesus, Savior, [G7] pilot [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] When at last I [F] near the [C] shore,
And the fearful [G7] breakers [C] roar
'Twixt me and the [F] peaceful [C] land,
Still supported [G7] by Thy [C] hand,
May I hear Thee [F] say to [C] me,
"Fear not, I will [G7] pilot [C] thee."
{end_of_verse}
